## Bill Splitter
// Who owes what after a meal:  each person pays for what they ordered, and their share of the tip.
// Change a name, an amount or the tip, and every sum follows.
// What's where, top to bottom:
//   money:  an amount written as dollars and cents
//   the bill splitter:  its diners, the tip, the sums, and its drawing
//   a diner:  their name, what they ordered, and what they owe
//   start
//   tests


## Money:  an amount as dollars and cents, e.g. 12.5 => "$12.50"
to write (amount as a number) as money:
	set cents to round (amount * 100)
	set dollars to (cents / 100) as an integer
	set left over to cents - dollars * 100
	if left over < 10 return "$" + dollars + ".0" + left over
	return "$" + dollars + "." + left over


## The bill splitter
bill splitter is an app where:
	- its "diners" is a new table
	// the tip, as a percent of what was ordered, e.g. 18
	- its "percent" is a number

	// what everyone ordered, added up
	- its "subtotal" is:
		set added up to 0
		for each diner in its diners
			set added up to added up + the amount of the diner
		return added up
	- its "tip" is its subtotal * its percent / 100
	- its "total" is its subtotal + its tip

	// an empty row, for the next person
	- to add someone:
		add (a new diner with name = "", amount = 0) to its diners

	// the tip, the diners, then the sums
	- to draw it:
		return <div class="BillSplitter">
			<h2>Bill Splitter</h2>
			<ui-form value={it}>
				<div class="Tip">
					<label>Tip</label>
					<ui-input name="percent" type="number" min="0" step="1" aria-label="Tip percent" label="%" labeled="right"/>
					<ui-buttons size="small" basic>
						<ui-button onClick={set its percent to 15}>15%</ui-button>
						<ui-button onClick={set its percent to 18}>18%</ui-button>
						<ui-button onClick={set its percent to 20}>20%</ui-button>
					</ui-buttons>
				</div>
			</ui-form>
			{draw its diners}
			<ui-button basic icon="plus" onClick={add someone}>Add someone</ui-button>
			<ui-segment>
				<div class="Sums">
					<div>Ordered</div><div>{write its subtotal as money}</div>
					<div>Tip</div><div>{write its tip as money}</div>
					<div class="Total">Total</div><div class="Total">{write its total as money}</div>
				</div>
			</ui-segment>
		</div>


## A diner:  their name, what they ordered, and what they owe
a "diner" is a view where:
	- its "name" is text
	// what they ordered, before the tip
	- its "amount" is a number
	// their share of the tip:  the same part of it as their part of the bill
	- its "tip" is its amount * the percent of bill splitter / 100
	- its "share" is its amount + its tip

	// a form of its own, bound to it:  typing a name or an amount changes the diner
	- to draw it:
		return <ui-form value={it}>
			<div part="row">
				<ui-input part="name" name="name" placeholder="Name" aria-label="Name" fluid/>
				<ui-input part="amount" name="amount" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" aria-label="Amount" label="$" fluid/>
				<div part="share">{write its share as money}</div>
				<ui-button part="remove" icon="close" basic aria-label="Remove" onClick={remove it}/>
			</div>
		</ui-form>

## The table:  the diners, one a row
a "table" is a viewable list of diners where:
	- to draw its placeholder:
		return <div part="placeholder">Nobody yet:  add someone</div>

// a diner sits at one table
a diner belongs to one table

// takes them off the bill
to remove (a diner):
	remove the diner from the diners of bill splitter


## Start
set the percent of bill splitter to 18
add (a new diner with name = "Ana", amount = 24) to the diners of bill splitter
add (a new diner with name = "Ben", amount = 18.5) to the diners of bill splitter
add (a new diner with name = "Cleo", amount = 31.25) to the diners of bill splitter
start bill splitter


## Tests
to test money
	write 12.5 as money should be "$12.50"
	write 3.07 as money should be "$3.07"
	write 0 as money should be "$0.00"
